From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 03:51:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 25/25] Fix a real pada_patha parsing bug found while
 diagnosing beyond RV 1.1

While waiting on the Round-4 external answer, ran the existing
reconstruct_chain() checker against RV 1.1-1.10 as a pure diagnostic --
not an attempt to scale the committed Krama generator's output, which
stays gated on the lead's own "only after" decision.

Found DGE's own pada_patha uses "iti" as an editorial disambiguation
gloss on the word immediately before it (541+76+1 times in Mandala 1),
completely separate from a real, independent "iti" word (a quotative
particle) that also occurs 12 times in the same corpus -- confirming
the same distinction the Q2 investigation two days ago reasoned out
from the sutra text alone. regenerate_krama_rv_1_1.py's word-splitter
was treating the whole gloss token as one literal (wrong) word (e.g.
feeding samhita_join the string "vaayo iti" as a single Pada word).

Fixed with _strip_pada_iti_gloss(), derived from all 3 shapes actually
observed in the corpus, including one genuine data quirk (a missing
danda merging two independent words into one token). RV 1.1 has zero
instances of this pattern -- confirmed the fix is a strict no-op there
(krama_regenerated_output.json byte-for-byte unchanged) and a real
improvement elsewhere (the diagnostic's own match rate against RV
1.1-1.10 went from 77/204 to 96/204 ardharcas from this one fix alone).

The actual scaling blocker was identified but deliberately not
attempted: split_into_ardharcas()'s automatic ardharca-boundary
detector has a much higher failure rate outside RV 1.1 (most of the
remaining 108 mismatches trace to the wrong split point, not a
phonology bug) -- a structural question for the scaling gate itself,
recorded in sec.10 with real numbers rather than worked around
mid-diagnostic.

New tests/test_pada_iti_gloss.py (7 tests). Full detail in
dge/RV_PRATISHAKHYA_KRAMA_ARCHITECTURE.md sec.6.15.

